---
title: Snowy owl
---
# Snowy owl

The snowy owl is a large white predator of the arctic tundra, the male almost
unmarked and the female heavily barred. Because the arctic summer has no
darkness at all it forages in broad daylight there, and reverts to preying in
the dark hours when it moves south for the winter. Lemmings dominate its diet,
and breeding success follows the lemming cycle so closely that a pair may not
lay at all in a poor year. See [[strigidae]].
